{"id":"n-20261009-8r6d2r","category":"tech","display_title":"Microsoft Unveils Surface Laptop Ultra","display_title_he":"מיקרוסופט חושפת את סרפס לפטופ אולטרה","short_summary":"Microsoft has introduced the Surface Laptop Ultra, a powerful new computer powered by an Nvidia AI chip designed to run local artificial intelligence models.","english_level":"C1","words":440,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"CNBC","domain":"cnbc.com","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/07/microsoft-starts-taking-preorders-for-2599-surface-laptop-ultra.html","title":"Microsoft to sell $2,599 Surface Laptop Ultra containing Nvidia AI chip","published_at":"2026-10-08T11:49:39.000Z"},{"name":"Geektime","domain":"geektime.co.il","url":"https://www.geektime.co.il/microsoft-surface-laptop-ultra-rtx-spark","title":"ראש בראש במקבוק פרו: מיקרוסופט ואנבידיה חושפות את Surface Laptop Ultra שיכול להריץ מודלי AI","published_at":"2026-10-08T07:22:34.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-08T07:22:34.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-09T06:30:10.104Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Microsoft has officially announced its new Surface Laptop Ultra, priced starting at $2,599, as the software maker tries to bring more artificial intelligence capabilities to consumer devices. The device is currently available for preorder and is scheduled to begin shipping on October 16, according to Pavan Davuluri, Microsoft's executive vice president of Windows and devices, who spoke at a company event in San Francisco. Designed to compete directly with Apple's MacBook Pro, the new hardware is tailored for developers, content creators, editors, and gamers who want to execute complex AI workloads locally rather than depending entirely on cloud services.","Beneath the aluminum chassis, the computer features an Nvidia RTX Spark N1X processor based on ARM architecture, developed in collaboration with Nvidia. During the event, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang noted that the Blackwell series graphic processing unit inside the machine delivers computing power equivalent to the company's 2016 DGX-1 data center server, which cost $250 million at the time. Furthermore, the hardware supplies up to one petaflop of computing power, allowing the device to run local artificial intelligence models containing over 120 billion parameters, including deep learning models such as DeepSeek v4 Flash with 280 billion parameters and Microsoft's own MAI Code 1.1 Flash with 137 billion parameters.","The hardware specifications also include a 15-inch HDR touchscreen capable of reaching a peak brightness of 2,000 nits, while weighing approximately 4.4 pounds or two kilograms. Notably, the laptop incorporates the world's first magnetic USB-C charging connector, resembling Apple's MagSafe system, alongside two standard USB-C ports, a USB-A port, a normal HDMI connection, a full-size SD card reader, and a standard audio jack. Base configurations of the device start with 24GB of unified memory, an 18-core processor, and 512GB of storage, whereas top-tier models can scale up to 128GB of unified memory, a 20-core processor, and 1TB of storage.","During a demonstration, Microsoft showed how the laptop can handle demanding tasks, such as running editing software like DaVinci Resolve alongside a newly released game at sixty frames per second. In comparisons presented on stage, the new hardware was shown to be faster than the M5 Pro MacBook Pro in generating tokens, images, and videos. To support software developers, Microsoft is updating Windows 11 to include routing capabilities that distribute artificial intelligence tasks between the local GPU and the cloud, indicated by a green leaf icon. Users will also be able to utilize quick setup for open-source software like OpenClaw and Meta's Muse AI agent, which is arriving in a native version for Windows. Additionally, Microsoft introduced secure Microsoft Execution Containers to prevent unwanted system access, alongside a trade-in program offering up to $1,000 in store credit for customers trading in a 16-inch MacBook Pro."],"facts":[{"fact":"Microsoft announced the Surface Laptop Ultra starting at $2,599, featuring an Nvidia AI chip.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The laptop is available for preorder and begins shipping on October 16.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"It includes the world's first magnetic USB-C charging port alongside standard USB-C ports.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The device contains an Nvidia Blackwell RTX Spark GPU built on ARM architecture.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang stated the GPU has processing power comparable to the 2016 DGX-1 data center server.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The laptop features a 15-inch HDR touchscreen with a maximum brightness of 2,000 nits and weighs about 4.4 pounds.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Base configurations include 24GB of unified memory and an 18-core processor, while top configurations include 128GB of unified memory.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Microsoft is introducing features to route AI tasks between the local GPU and the cloud.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Meta will introduce a Windows version of its Muse AI agent.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Microsoft offers a trade-in program providing up to $1,000 credit for a 16-inch MacBook Pro with an M5 Pro chip.","sources":[2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Microsoft","lemma":"Microsoft","pos":"noun","he":"מיקרוסופט","name":"true"},{"text":"has officially announced","lemma":"officially announce","pos":"verb","he":"הכריזה רשמית","name":false},{"text":"its new Surface Laptop Ultra","lemma":"Surface Laptop Ultra","pos":"noun","he":"סרפס לפטופ אולטרה החדש שלה","name":false},{"text":"priced starting","lemma":"price start","pos":"verb","he":"מתומחר החל מ-","name":false},{"text":"as the software maker","lemma":"software maker","pos":"noun","he":"בעוד יצרנית התוכנה","name":false},{"text":"tries to bring","lemma":"try to bring","pos":"verb","he":"מנסה להביא","